p.src:
The first abstraction arrives when the speaker says that he could take a box out to a device and have devices talk to each other. Here the lecture moves from examples to mechanism: $\text{device programming}
\;\to\;
\text{devices talk to each other}
\;\to\;
\text{protocols}.$ That word, protocols, is the hinge. Once it enters, the skill is no longer merely local programming. It is now a way of organizing communication across components.

