p.src:
The lecture then widens the same chain one step further: $\text{protocols}
\;\to\;
\text{working with companies and people}.$ This is the real payload of the early technical work. Devices talking to each other teach more than software or hardware. They teach interfaces, coordination, and the human systems that must make technical systems function.

